<title>GERMANY: W.German July industry output +0.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W.German July industry output +0.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT   July 96    June 96    July 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.5	 unch	 +1.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -1.7	 -0.8	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		95.8	 95.3	 97.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. @</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				  July 96		  June 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     84.9	 -3.3     87.8	 -0.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   94.5	 unch     94.5	 +0.7</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   97.5	 -0.1     97.6	 +0.9</p>
<p>	Capital goods     94.9	 +1.6     93.4	 +1.1</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 86.6	 +2.5     84.5	 +2.9</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    90.7	 -3.3     93.8	 -1.7</p>
<p> Energy output	   109.6	 unch    109.6	 +0.7</p>
<p> Construction	    102.2	 +7.2     95.3	 -2.4 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison June/July 96 with April/May 96:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    +1.0 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison June/July 96 with June/July 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     -0.9</p>
<p> Mining				    -6.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 -0.5</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     -2.0</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +2.0</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	+2.6</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -1.8</p>
<p> Energy output			   +4.8</p>
<p> Construction			    -7.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
